{title: God Bless Our Native Land}
{artist: Siegfried August Mahlmann · tr. Charles Timothy Brooks & John Sullivan Dwight}
{key: F}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
God bless our native land! Firm may she ever stand Through storm and
night; When the wild tempests rave, Ruler of wind and wave,
Do Thou our country save By Thy great might.

Verse 2
For her our prayer shall rise To God above the skies; On Him we
wait; Thou who art ever nigh, Guarding with watchful eye,
To Thee aloud we cry, God save the state!
